Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimeUrbanDrivingWithSlowVehicle" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:actor1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Yellow vehicle driving slowly in the center lane" .

:actor2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Red vehicle parked on the right side of the road" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Yellow lane markings and road surface" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Slow-moving yellow vehicle occupying center lane, potentially causing lane intrusion risk" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential rear-end collision risk due to slow-moving yellow vehicle in the center lane" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Occlusion risk due to parked red vehicle on the right side, potentially obscuring visibility" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.65"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.70"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.50"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Slow-moving yellow vehicle occupying center lane, potentially causing lane intrusion risk.
Severity Score: 0.65

**Risk 2:**
Description: Potential rear-end collision risk due to slow-moving yellow vehicle in the center lane.
Severity Score: 0.70

**Risk 3:**
Description: Occlusion risk due to parked red vehicle on the right side, potentially obscuring visibility.
Severity Score: 0.50

The scene is classified as a **BehaviorAnomaly** due to the unusual behavior of the yellow vehicle driving slowly in the center lane, which is not typical driving behavior in this context. The risks identified are based on the potential for lane intrusion, rear-end collision, and occlusion.